      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SWEETHEARTED (8) showed promise in a dominant debut win at this circuit and distance, where she was heavily backed into very short odds and won by a big margin. The second-row draw is a new obstacle, but the mile rate of 1:57.4 and the margin leave her clearly the one they must reach. KEAYANG MARICRUZ (7) has the right profile to test her, bringing a Kilmore maiden win two back before a Terang sixth in a 2& 0-1 WIN race run in 1:57.1. She resumes from five weeks off and Danielle Hill takes the drive, though the second-row draw makes the early stages important. HELENSHOPE (6) resumed with a sound third at Globe Derby Park, beaten just over six metres, and should be fitter second-up. JILLIBY ECLIPSE (4) won a 2 Lifetime Wins race at Gawler by 6.5m only two days ago, but her prior Globe Derby Park run included breaking stride at the first turn, so manners and the quick back-up are the decisive points for her.",
